#====================================================================
# DRAFT-libmad-0.15.1b-clang-gcc-only-optimization-flags
# 触发事件: libmad 0.15.1b HarmonyOS PC 适配（R01）
#          configure 生成的 CFLAGS 含 GCC 专属优化 flag，clang-15 不识别
#====================================================================

id:                     DRAFT-libmad-0.15.1b-clang-gcc-only-optimization-flags
trigger_tool:           configure|clang|make
phase:                  configuration|compilation
error_signature: 'unrecognized.*option.*-fforce-mem|unrecognized.*option.*-fexpensive-optimizations|
                    unknown argument.*-fforce-mem|unknown argument.*-fregmove|optimize=.*-fthread-jumps|
                    cc1: error: unrecognized command-line option'

severity:               2
category:               ohos|autotools|clang|gcc-flags|portability
match_keywords:         fforce-mem, fforce-addr, fthread-jumps, fcse-follow-jumps,
                         fcse-skip-blocks, fexpensive-optimizations, fregmove,
                         fschedule-insns2, GCC, clang, configure, optimize,
                         OHOS, HarmonyOS, autotools, CFLAGS

title: 'GCC-only optimization flags embedded in configure break clang toolchains'

root_cause: >
  Old autotools projects (GCC 3.x era, e.g. libmad 2004) hardcode GCC-only optimization
  flags in the configure script's optimize variable, e.g.
  `optimize="$optimize -fforce-mem -fforce-addr -fthread-jumps -fcse-follow-jumps
  -fcse-skip-blocks -fexpensive-optimizations -fregmove -fschedule-insns2"`.
  Clang (including OHOS clang-15) does not support these historical GCC flags and rejects
  them at compile time. The failure looks like the toolchain being broken, but the real
  cause is configure injecting unsupported flags into CFLAGS.

affected_scope: >
  Any autotools project from the GCC 2.95/3.x era ported to a clang-based toolchain
  (OHOS PC clang-15, and other clang cross toolchains). libmad, minimad, and similar
  media/DSP libraries of that vintage are typical.

verification_cmd: |
  grep -n 'fforce-mem\|fexpensive-optimizations' configure
  ./configure --enable-static --disable-shared
  make -j1

solution: >
  In the Conan recipe build() (or equivalent patch step), delete each
  `optimize="$optimize <flag>"` line from configure with replace_in_file BEFORE running
  configure. The flags are pure historical GCC hints with no effect on modern
  optimization; removing them is safe. Do not pass -Wno-* (unrecognized option is not a
  warning) and do not disable optimization entirely.

rec_approach:           patch-configure-strip-gcc-only-flags
rec_priority:           1
rec_auto_fix:           true

validation: >
  After stripping, configure + make complete without unknown-option errors; the library
  builds and the OHOS-specific decode test produces valid output (libmad: 1152 PCM
  samples per MPEG frame).

boundary_notes: >
  Only flags actually rejected by clang need removal; shared flags (-O2 -fPIC) must be
  preserved. Recheck per project since the exact flag set is version-dependent.

knowledge_dedup_seven_axes:
  exact_duplicate: "false"
  causal_duplicate: "false"
  trigger_overlap: "false"
  solution_overlap: "false"
  combination_novelty: "true"
  boundary_novelty: "true"
  test_migration_novelty: "true"
  similar_to: "E063(-Werror), E205(config.guess/config.sub OHOS)"
  caused_by: "none"
  prerequisite_of: "none"
  conflicts_with: "none"

